From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:24:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: drop the per-fragment-job signal with sync elision

Each fragment job ended with a deferred SYNC_ADD64 on the fragment
subqueue's sync object. Waits on the fragment subqueue target barrier
signals (or owed sync points), which come after waiting for its earlier
jobs, so these signals only numbered sync points nothing waits for, at
~2 us of command stream frontend time per render pass. All subqueues
share that time, so it was paid on every pass.

With sync elision, don't emit them, nor load the sync object address
they use. To keep sync point 0 of the next command buffer covering all
earlier fragment work, the end of the command buffer (and
vkCmdExecuteCommands()) emits one signal deferred until the fragment
iterators are idle when jobs ran unsignaled. Secondary command buffers
keep the per-job signal.

The sync elision check moves to panvk_cmd_buffer.h so the draw code can
use it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: drop the deferred sync object signal after each fragment job in primary command buffers (nothing waits on those sync points); one deferred signal at the end of the command buffer keeps sync point 0 covering all fragment work
Upstream-commit: none (generic PanVK CSF; upstream candidate)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: rg477m/010
Validation test: drawbench pass tests 7-15% faster (loadpasses, indep, passes, mixclear), draws unchanged, image checksums unchanged; Hades Vulkan renderer 1255 MHz 173.1 -> 177.9 fps (A-B-B-A); Hades DXVK 103.3 -> 104.2 fps at 502 MHz; Serious Sam D3D11 46.8 -> 48.2, Vulkan 53.2 -> 52.9 fps; racetest all cases 0/100 stale, controls 100/100; PanProbe 38/38; no GPU faults
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
